WEBVTT

00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:56.741
Wake up, brats!

00:01:56.741 --> 00:01:57.867
Time for night practice.

00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:00.286
Practice swings. Ten thousand
of 'em. Get going!

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.621
Practice?

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.832
In the middle of the night?

00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:06.167
You trash think you can beat

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:09.004
the winners without practicing at night?

00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:15.844
I can't believe we have to practice now.

00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:17.345
It's raining.

00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:20.724
Hey, you three.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:22.517
Hold up.

00:02:23.018 --> 00:02:24.352
You three?

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:26.146
Us?

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:29.524
I've got an important mission for you.

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:31.568
What sort of mission?

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:34.988
Through here. You'll see.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:47.000
"Special Mission"

00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:53.131
This cave goes pretty deep.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.760
I'm so tired.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.804
Hey, there's something up ahead.

00:03:00.347 --> 00:03:02.307
"Special Mission"

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:03.933
"Special Mission"
A letter?

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.811
This is it. This is our special mission.

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:15.028
Well? What does it say?

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.614
This one's gonna be dicey.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.784
You mean it's a dangerous mission?

00:03:21.242 --> 00:03:24.704
Better make sure we're fixed up
before we walk in there.

00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:27.290
You mean we'd better prepare ourselves?

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.208
I see.

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:30.627
So, what does it say?

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:36.549
We gotta go to the camp
and filch some swag.

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:40.470
Go to the camp and... What?

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.390
Filch some swag.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.643
Filch... some swag.

00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:47.977
How am I supposed to get this?

00:03:47.977 --> 00:03:49.354
Is this a test?

00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:50.355
Come on!

00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:51.231
Echizen, you read it!

00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:55.026
Let's see...

00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:58.154
"The following is your mission.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.953
First, mission one, you will
sneak into the camp

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:07.247
and acquire the following items
from the practice storage shed:

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:11.334
100 new tennis balls, 50 bars of soap,

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.713
and 10 bottles of both
shampoo and conditioner.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:21.052
Afterwards, you will go
to the staff bar lounge

00:04:21.052 --> 00:04:23.555
in the dorms and acquire
high quality sake.

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:26.307
Make this special
mission to acquire sake

00:04:26.307 --> 00:04:30.603
your top priority over
the balls or soap."

00:04:31.646 --> 00:04:32.939
In other words,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.608
he wants us to steal some
sake from the dorms.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.526
What is he thinking?

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.488
Why'd he choose us three for the job?

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:44.993
"You may be wondering why I chose you."

00:04:44.993 --> 00:04:47.078
What? How'd he know?

00:04:47.078 --> 00:04:48.955
That coach must be psychic.

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:51.583
"When selecting you,

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.543
your ultimate balance of personalities,

00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:55.045
physical abilities,

00:04:55.045 --> 00:05:01.468
and flexible, quick decision
making in dangerous situations...

00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:04.304
...were not deciding factors, but rather,

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:08.224
I chose you because you
happened to be there."

00:05:08.224 --> 00:05:09.642
That's it?!

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.310
Ow.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.355
"Incidentally, even if
you fail your mission

00:05:13.355 --> 00:05:16.066
and get yourselves into trouble,

00:05:16.066 --> 00:05:18.401
the powers that be will
not be concerned.

00:05:18.401 --> 00:05:20.820
Best of luck on your mission.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:25.575
Also, this letter will self
destruct in five seconds."

00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:29.412
Self destruct? He can't mean...

00:05:29.412 --> 00:05:30.997
It's gonna explode?

00:05:40.256 --> 00:05:42.133
Of course it won't.

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:48.556
Are those...

00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:51.393
Bats!

00:05:52.769 --> 00:05:54.145
Bats?

00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:57.273
When he said self destruct...

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:59.150
...is this what he meant?

00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:07.909
This doesn't look good.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.336
Run!

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.637
Crap. It's a dead end.

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:40.442
I've always thought,
despite your appearance,

00:06:40.442 --> 00:06:44.404
you're pretty agile, Tanishi-<i>san</i>.

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:46.156
What was that?

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:48.908
Not bad, guys.

00:06:51.828 --> 00:06:53.913
I won't lose to you.

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:58.418
Let Naniwa's Speed Star

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:02.881
show you how to leap across rocks.

00:07:03.173 --> 00:07:04.007
Oops.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:07.427
Kenya-<i>san</i>!

00:07:09.554 --> 00:07:14.517
I might be faster than you,
but my balance is terrible!

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.645
But you're running on water.

00:07:18.146 --> 00:07:20.607
Grab on!

00:07:23.568 --> 00:07:25.403
Kenya-<i>san</i>, just a little more.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:33.703
I'm at my limit.

00:07:35.205 --> 00:07:36.122
Oshitari!

00:07:55.225 --> 00:07:56.267
Hey...

00:07:56.267 --> 00:07:57.936
Did everyone make it?

00:08:00.772 --> 00:08:03.775
Are we...

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:06.319
Yeah. This is...

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:10.281
We're inside the U-17 training camp.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.958
What is all this?

00:08:20.291 --> 00:08:23.586
Has the security always been this tight?

00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:25.964
Echizen?

00:08:25.964 --> 00:08:29.509
You can't seriously be trying to
carry out Coach Mifune's mission.

00:08:30.844 --> 00:08:33.346
I'd understand if this were
some kind of training,

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:36.266
but there's no way this has
anything to do with tennis.

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:40.145
That's right. Why do we have
to snatch that stuff for him?

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:46.234
Yeah, but I can't stand the thought

00:08:47.444 --> 00:08:49.571
of telling Coach Mifune we couldn't do it.

00:08:51.698 --> 00:08:54.034
I guess so...

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:56.661
Those are Dobermans, though!

00:08:56.661 --> 00:08:58.038
They're not some common house dog.

00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:01.916
Then we'd better not get caught.

00:09:12.469 --> 00:09:16.931
Got 100 balls, soap,
shampoo, and conditioner.

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:19.267
Mission one complete.

00:09:19.809 --> 00:09:21.353
Next is...

00:09:21.853 --> 00:09:24.105
The special mission.

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:34.783
Calm down, Kenya-<i>san</i>.

00:09:36.326 --> 00:09:38.411
There's something wrong with that dog.

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:40.997
He ain't moving.

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:45.251
Huh? Don't tell me it's...

00:09:48.171 --> 00:09:49.464
It's a statue.

00:09:49.464 --> 00:09:51.508
Don't scare me like that.

00:09:51.508 --> 00:09:53.301
Let's get a move on.

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:04.604
Oh?

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.981
They're already here.

00:10:09.317 --> 00:10:14.447
Ow. That Tsuge guy's a real sadist.

00:10:15.865 --> 00:10:17.492
How are you doing?

00:10:17.492 --> 00:10:19.869
I finally managed to master it.

00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:22.789
I need to keep practicing, though.

00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:25.875
The high schoolers aren't practicing

00:10:25.875 --> 00:10:27.711
at this hour, are they?

00:10:28.086 --> 00:10:29.170
You're right.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.383
There's no point in learning the spell
if you can't use it when you need it.

00:10:33.758 --> 00:10:35.051
Spell?

00:10:35.051 --> 00:10:36.344
What are they talking about?

00:10:37.178 --> 00:10:41.599
I still can't believe
this camp is haunted.

00:10:41.599 --> 00:10:44.352
I didn't believe it at first either,

00:10:44.352 --> 00:10:46.104
but apparently it's true.

00:10:46.563 --> 00:10:48.023
Around this time every year,

00:10:48.023 --> 00:10:52.235
someone always sees the
ghost of the deserter.

00:10:52.235 --> 00:10:55.739
A ghost? Of a deserter?

00:10:55.739 --> 00:10:57.115
What the hell is that?

00:10:57.115 --> 00:11:00.368
During the warring states period,
there was a battle here.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.246
A foot soldier fled the
battle, but he met a

00:11:03.246 --> 00:11:05.123
brutal end at the hands of
some deserter hunters.

00:11:05.665 --> 00:11:09.919
And his severed head
appears as a ghost now?

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:14.966
Yeah, but if you recite the spell,
he'll leave you alone.

00:11:15.967 --> 00:11:18.386
Let's take it from the top again.

00:11:18.386 --> 00:11:19.346
Yeah.

00:11:19.637 --> 00:11:23.308
Ready, and... Step, step,
one, two, one, two.

00:11:23.308 --> 00:11:25.560
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.062
--Step, step,
one, two, one, two.

00:11:27.062 --> 00:11:28.146
--Ghost of the deserter? That's stupid.
--Step, step,
one, two, one, two.

00:11:28.146 --> 00:11:29.314
--Ghost of the deserter? That's stupid.
--Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:11:29.314 --> 00:11:30.315
--Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:11:30.315 --> 00:11:32.817
Step, step,
one, two, one, two...

00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:38.740
The bar lounge should
be up ahead, but...

00:11:39.949 --> 00:11:42.327
That's gonna be a problem.

00:11:43.119 --> 00:11:46.247
It's impossible to get through
without being seen by the cameras.

00:11:47.749 --> 00:11:52.712
If only there was a box of space
the camera couldn't see.

00:11:52.712 --> 00:11:54.964
There's no way we'll find one.

00:11:57.342 --> 00:11:59.010
Box.

00:12:06.017 --> 00:12:09.646
You moron, he didn't
mean that literally.

00:12:13.191 --> 00:12:14.693
Nice, Tanishi-<i>san</i>.

00:12:19.989 --> 00:12:22.909
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:12:22.909 --> 00:12:27.122
These squares seem to be those
cameras' only blind spots.

00:12:27.122 --> 00:12:30.959
You're saying that was a hint?

00:12:30.959 --> 00:12:32.961
Who'd bother with all of this?

00:12:33.628 --> 00:12:34.796
I dunno.

00:12:34.796 --> 00:12:37.465
Perhaps someone who likes this
sort of thing set it up.

00:12:38.967 --> 00:12:42.137
If that's the case,
he must be a real weirdo.

00:12:55.108 --> 00:12:59.154
Two, five, nine... one, one, three.

00:13:00.321 --> 00:13:02.949
One, one, three...

00:13:04.701 --> 00:13:05.618
It opened.

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:10.832
This year's challengers
are quite skilled.

00:13:11.666 --> 00:13:15.295
However, will they be able
to clear the final barrier?

00:13:24.012 --> 00:13:25.930
The bar lounge.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.599
We're finally here.

00:13:27.599 --> 00:13:29.934
Time to complete the special mission.

00:13:33.355 --> 00:13:35.732
Let's grab some sake
and get out of here.

00:13:35.732 --> 00:13:37.108
Let's go!

00:13:37.108 --> 00:13:38.777
Wait, Kenya-<i>san</i>, Tanishi-<i>san</i>.

00:13:42.447 --> 00:13:43.948
The hell is this?

00:13:43.948 --> 00:13:47.535
I'm not sure, but I don't
think we should touch that.

00:13:47.535 --> 00:13:49.329
Sure seems that way.

00:13:52.374 --> 00:13:54.668
Kenya-<i>san</i>, a little higher.

00:13:55.919 --> 00:13:58.254
Your head. Your head's
almost touching it.

00:13:59.005 --> 00:14:01.216
Careful. One's coming from the left.

00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:06.346
No, no. We can't do this.

00:14:06.346 --> 00:14:09.391
You can't get through no
matter how flexible you are.

00:14:09.391 --> 00:14:10.809
This sucks.

00:14:10.809 --> 00:14:13.144
We almost had it, too.

00:14:13.144 --> 00:14:14.729
Oh, come on.

00:14:14.729 --> 00:14:18.108
The target of our special
mission is right there.

00:14:25.031 --> 00:14:28.618
Where are my legs?

00:14:28.618 --> 00:14:31.579
Where is my right hand?

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.040
Around this time every year,

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:38.253
someone always sees the
ghost of the deserter.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:41.172
A foot soldier fled the
battle, but he met a

00:14:41.172 --> 00:14:43.008
brutal end at the hands of
some deserter hunters.

00:14:44.134 --> 00:14:49.514
Is this the ghost of the deserter
they were talking about?

00:14:51.057 --> 00:14:53.351
My legs are gone.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:57.022
Where is my right hand?

00:14:58.356 --> 00:15:02.068
Ghost of the deserter? That's stupid.

00:15:02.068 --> 00:15:04.863
I'm not afraid of him.

00:15:04.863 --> 00:15:06.990
There's no way he exists.

00:15:08.491 --> 00:15:11.369
But... where are my legs?

00:15:11.369 --> 00:15:13.038
Keep them there.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.291
Where's my right hand?

00:15:16.291 --> 00:15:17.417
In front of you.

00:15:17.417 --> 00:15:18.710
Put your hand on the ground.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.590
No. You've gotta twist your body more.

00:15:27.677 --> 00:15:30.221
My side's cramping, my side's cramping!

00:15:30.221 --> 00:15:32.682
Don't give up. Give it another go.

00:15:32.682 --> 00:15:35.310
I don't wanna hear it, Tanishi!

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:40.106
Even without the lasers,
you'd barely fit down that hallway.

00:15:40.106 --> 00:15:41.858
What'd you say?!

00:15:41.858 --> 00:15:43.401
It's true.

00:15:44.319 --> 00:15:47.405
Can you wait until after we're done?

00:15:47.405 --> 00:15:48.865
Shut up!

00:15:48.865 --> 00:15:51.659
This mission doesn't have
anything to do with tennis.

00:15:51.659 --> 00:15:53.244
Frankly, I don't give a crap.

00:15:53.244 --> 00:15:55.330
Yeah. Who cares?

00:15:57.999 --> 00:15:59.334
Quiet down, you guys.

00:15:59.334 --> 00:16:00.835
What?

00:16:00.835 --> 00:16:02.337
Someone's coming.

00:16:04.005 --> 00:16:06.549
Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:06.549 --> 00:16:08.927
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:10.095 --> 00:16:12.806
Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:12.806 --> 00:16:15.517
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.894
--Is that Akaya Kirihara's voice?

00:16:17.894 --> 00:16:18.687
--Step, step, one, two, one, two.
--Is that Akaya Kirihara's voice?

00:16:18.687 --> 00:16:20.605
--Step, step, one, two, one, two.
--What's he saying?

00:16:20.605 --> 00:16:22.607
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:22.607 --> 00:16:23.108
--Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:23.108 --> 00:16:25.485
--The winners must be training so
hard that Kirihara finally snapped.
--Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:25.485 --> 00:16:27.570
--The winners must be training so
hard that Kirihara finally snapped.
--Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:30.323
--The winners must be training so
hard that Kirihara finally snapped.
--Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:30.323 --> 00:16:32.951
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:34.828 --> 00:16:39.207
Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:39.666 --> 00:16:42.002
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:42.002 --> 00:16:44.629
You're spouting that
crap, too, Echizen?

00:16:45.255 --> 00:16:48.425
Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:16:48.425 --> 00:16:51.261
Turn and Ina Bauer.

00:16:52.095 --> 00:16:53.304
We can get through.

00:16:54.347 --> 00:16:56.558
We can get through the lasers.

00:16:56.933 --> 00:16:58.018
What do you mean?

00:16:58.518 --> 00:17:01.187
If we move according to
Kirihara-<i>san</i>'s instructions,

00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:03.648
we can pass through
without touching the lasers.

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.155
Are you ready?

00:17:11.031 --> 00:17:12.490
Ready any time.

00:17:12.949 --> 00:17:15.201
Tanishi-<i>san</i>, wait over here.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:16.953
Sure.

00:17:17.787 --> 00:17:18.663
Let's go.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:22.208
Step, step, one, two, one, two.

00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:24.336
Turn, and Ina Bauer.

00:17:24.711 --> 00:17:25.754
Amazing!

00:17:26.921 --> 00:17:29.049
Kenya-<i>san</i>, that's it.

00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:30.008
Yeah.

00:17:31.217 --> 00:17:32.010
Kick.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:32.761
Punch.

00:17:32.761 --> 00:17:33.928
Ina Bauer.

00:17:33.928 --> 00:17:35.138
Axe kick.

00:17:35.138 --> 00:17:39.851
Ina Bauer.

00:17:39.851 --> 00:17:42.187
There are too many Ina Bauers!

00:17:45.398 --> 00:17:46.775
We did it.

00:17:46.775 --> 00:17:48.860
We made it through the trap.

00:17:51.071 --> 00:17:55.742
But why'd Kirihara give us that hint?

00:17:55.742 --> 00:17:58.995
Who knows? Either way, we should hurry.

00:17:58.995 --> 00:17:59.954
Yeah.

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.540
Tanishi, keep watch over there.

00:18:04.834 --> 00:18:06.252
All right.

00:18:06.252 --> 00:18:07.962
Now all we have to do is get the sake,

00:18:07.962 --> 00:18:09.506
and our mission will be complete.

00:18:11.883 --> 00:18:14.094
I'm kinda hungry.

00:18:14.844 --> 00:18:16.930
Kenya-<i>san</i>, look.

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:28.566
Delicious. This ham is the best.

00:18:28.566 --> 00:18:30.276
There are sausages over here.

00:18:30.276 --> 00:18:32.654
What're you chowing down on? Hurry up.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.448
They've even got fruit.

00:18:35.865 --> 00:18:37.742
So good. It's so good.

00:18:37.742 --> 00:18:39.327
This is ecstasy.

00:18:41.746 --> 00:18:44.416
Let's do this!

00:19:21.369 --> 00:19:22.495
Oh, well.

00:19:24.831 --> 00:19:26.207
Tanishi, you moron!

00:19:26.207 --> 00:19:27.709
What are you doing?!

00:19:27.709 --> 00:19:29.753
It ain't fair if it's only you two.

00:19:29.753 --> 00:19:31.129
Come on.

00:19:31.588 --> 00:19:33.548
We gotta get out of here.

00:19:33.882 --> 00:19:36.426
Echizen, get the sake in the gourd.

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:39.137
Echizen, what are you doing?

00:19:39.846 --> 00:19:41.973
This belongs to my senpai.

00:19:41.973 --> 00:19:44.392
Inui

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:49.564
This is Inui's special vegetable juice.

00:19:50.482 --> 00:19:55.528
Who knows how many victims
this Inui juice has claimed?

00:19:56.237 --> 00:19:59.032
What's this doing here?

00:19:59.657 --> 00:20:02.118
I've got an idea.

00:20:02.118 --> 00:20:03.828
What kind of idea?

00:20:03.828 --> 00:20:05.413
You don't mean...

00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:12.671
Die, Coach Mifune!

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:15.840
Mission accomplished!

00:20:16.633 --> 00:20:18.593
I was getting sick of waiting, idiots.

00:20:18.593 --> 00:20:20.178
Reporting in, sir.

00:20:20.178 --> 00:20:21.930
We have 100 balls, 50 bars of soap...

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.099
Enough. I don't care about that crap.

00:20:24.099 --> 00:20:25.433
Gimme my gourd.

00:20:25.934 --> 00:20:28.770
I was worried I wouldn't
get this before dawn.

00:20:54.754 --> 00:20:56.381
Good work.

00:21:00.927 --> 00:21:02.220
Is there a problem?

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:03.638
N-No.

00:21:03.972 --> 00:21:06.558
Um, excuse us.

00:21:09.602 --> 00:21:13.398
Hey, Echizen. You put Inui
juice in there, right?

00:21:13.773 --> 00:21:15.483
I know I did.

00:21:15.483 --> 00:21:18.278
Then why isn't anything
happening to him?

00:21:18.653 --> 00:21:21.031
He's a monster.

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.658
Hold on, idiots.

00:21:25.285 --> 00:21:29.039
Leave all the sausage, salami, and ham

00:21:29.039 --> 00:21:30.623
you have in your pockets.

00:21:30.623 --> 00:21:34.085
Uh, what are you talking about?

00:21:34.461 --> 00:21:36.004
Leave them.

00:21:37.464 --> 00:21:39.215
I'm sorry!

00:21:39.674 --> 00:21:41.509
We still have a long way to go.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:18.606
"Preview"

00:23:18.606 --> 00:23:20.608
"Preview"
Damn it, what kind of
stupid hunt is this?

00:23:20.608 --> 00:23:20.900
Damn it, what kind of
stupid hunt is this?

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:22.402
Calm down, Shishido-<i>kun</i>.

00:23:22.402 --> 00:23:24.863
We just have to keep cool
and run from that eagle.

00:23:24.863 --> 00:23:27.615
That's right. If he pops
your balloon, you're out.

00:23:27.615 --> 00:23:30.660
I know that, but what's
the point of doing this?

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:32.912
He must have us do this for
more than his entertainment.

00:23:32.912 --> 00:23:36.875
Huh? That's right.
We climbed that cliff so easily.

00:23:36.875 --> 00:23:39.294
We're improving.

00:23:42.005 --> 00:23:43.548
"Evolution and Change"
The next episode of <i>Prince of Tennis II</i>
is: "Evolution and Change."

00:23:43.548 --> 00:23:47.136
"Evolution and Change"
There's something suspicious
about that coach.
